  "backtest_data_needs": "tick",
  "python_conversion_notes": "The ZigZag indicator must be reimplemented in Python or sourced from a library (e.g., zigzag pip package). The Fibonacci 57% level is non-standard and must be hardcoded. Pending order lifecycle with timed deletion needs explicit state management in Python. The EMA crossover uses previous bar values (index [1]) not current, which is important for backtest alignment. The ZigZag 'skip 5 bars' heuristic to avoid repainting must be preserved. Stops level validation against broker SYMBOL_TRADE_STOPS_LEVEL must be handled. Lot size normalization (lotStep rounding) must be replicated.",
